    "narrative": "Our primary offensive engine for today\u2019s slate is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries an elite efficiency score of 73.66. Facing a middle-of-the-road matchup against Martinez, he benefits from a significant 14% boost via platoon splits and a prime spot in the #3 hole, positioning him to anchor our production in R and RBI. **Kyle Tucker** also serves as a high-floor asset with a 61.34 score despite his drop to the #8 spot in the order; the favorable park factors and the matchup against Mahle provide enough ceiling to ignore the suboptimal batting order placement. While **Sam Antonacci** sits just inside our \"Strong\" tier at 46.73, his leadoff placement against the tough Espino is a calculated risk, leveraging his high-leverage opportunities to drive value in a difficult matchup.\n\nOn the periphery, **Jackson Merrill** (54.13) and **Andy Pages** (50.82) are forced to shoulder a heavy burden against unfavorable SP skill ratings and platoon disadvantages. **Jackson Merrill** receives a nuanced boost from a slow-delivering pitcher, which we hope translates into a high-value stolen base to bolster our scarcest category. **Liam Hicks** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, narrowly falling short of the 40-point \"Marginal\" threshold with a 37.21 score; his decline was largely due to a harsh dynamic platoon penalty against Fried. We continue to manage our games-played caps carefully, opting to bench **Liam Hicks** rather than force a start that lacks clear statistical merit.\n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **Drake Baldwin** (43.58) and **Miguel Vargas** (40.76) facing a stern test against the elite Glasnow and Espino, respectively. Both players are hovering just above our \"Below Floor\" threshold, and we will monitor the situation closely to ensure they don't slide further should weather or late lineup shifts materialize. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** unavailable due to scheduling or injury, the current depth chart\u2014including **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias**\u2014must remain prepared to rotate in as we navigate the remainder of the season.",
